PaymentRails_WrapNative
├── when caller is not the owner
│   ├── it should revert with OwnableUnauthorizedAccount
│   └── it should leave both balances untouched
├── given native ingress is disabled
│   └── it should revert with PaymentRails_NativeNotSupported
├── given native balance is zero
│   └── it should revert with PaymentRails_ZeroNativeBalance
├── given the wrapper credits less than the deposit
│   ├── it should revert with PaymentRails_WrapAmountMismatch
│   └── it should leave the native balance untouched
└── given native balance is non-zero
    ├── it should return the wrapped amount
    ├── it should set the native balance to zero
    ├── it should increase the wrapped balance by exactly the native balance
    ├── it should move the native value into the wrapper
    ├── it should emit NativeWrapped with the owner and amount
    ├── given value arrived without calling receive
    │   └── it should wrap the forced balance too
    ├── when the wrapper re-enters wrapNative as the owner
    │   ├── it should block the re-entrant call with the reentrancy guard
    │   └── it should complete the outer call
    ├── when the wrapper re-enters wrapNative as a stranger
    │   ├── it should reject the re-entrant call as unauthorized
    │   └── it should complete the outer call
    ├── given wrappedNative is configured for an action
    │   └── it should route the wrapped balance through executeAction
    └── fuzz
        └── when native balance is any non-zero amount
            └── it should wrap exactly that amount
